-- title:
--   Frobenius parity of the decomposition group action via ψ₀
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $A_2$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A_2$ (so $A_2$ lies over $q$), and assume that its decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$ acts isometrically, i.e. $A_2.\mathrm{valuation}(\sigma x) = A_2.\mathrm{valuation}(x)$ for all $\sigma$ in $A_2.\mathrm{decompositionSubgroup}\ \mathbb{Q}$ and all $x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\chi$ be a homomorphism from that decomposition subgroup to $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/2)$ characterised by the property that $\chi(\tau) = 1$ exactly when $\tau$ fixes every element $x$ of the residue field of $A_2$ with $x^{q^2} = x$. Let $\mathcal{O}_0$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal{O}_0$ irreducible, $\mathcal{O}_0$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, $\mathrm{card}(\mathcal{O}_0/(\pi)) = q$ and $(q) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}_0$; assume $\mathcal{O}_0$ acts on $\mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2)$, the topological closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $A_2.\mathrm{valuation}$, making the latter the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}_0$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra, $Fr$ an $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it (so the residue field is algebraically closed), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{q}$ modulo it for all $x$. Let $\psi_0 : Onr \to$ the completion of $A_2.\mathrm{valuation}$ be a ring homomorphism whose restriction along $\mathcal{O}_0 \to Onr$ agrees with $\mathcal{O}_0 \to \mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2) \to$ the completion. Then for every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup there is $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $n = 0$ or $n = 1$ such that $\tau \cdot \psi_0(y) = \psi_0(Fr^{\,n}(y))$ for all $y \in Onr$ with $Fr(Fr(y)) = y$, and such that $n = 0$ if and only if $\chi(\tau) = 1$.
--
--   This records that the decomposition group at a place above $q$ acts, through $\psi_0$, on the $Fr^2$-fixed part of the unramified coefficient ring $Onr$ (the unramified quadratic lift) by a power of Frobenius whose exponent is the parity given by $\chi$. It is used in the read-off of the Mumford embedding on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side, being cited by the two theorems computing that embedding from a function-field equivalence for the ring homomorphisms sending the coordinates to $(1,0)$ and to $(0,1)$.
